          "title": "Valve Function: Preventing Backflow",
          "description": "Valves act like one-way doors during the cardiac cycle. Connect the valve type to the chamber separation: atrioventricular valves (tricuspid, mitral/bicuspid) prevent backflow between atria and ventricles, and semilunar valves (pulmonary, aortic) prevent backflow between ventricles and great arteries."
